{"id":"mahabharata-12-208","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":208,"title":"अष्टाधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 208 · Mastery of the senses","summary":{"en":"The teacher says that beings who are attached to the ills of the senses sink, while the one without attachment goes beyond. He tells how a man who controls the mind and senses is worshipped even by the gods and gains the eternal Brahman.","kn":"ಇಂದ್ರಿಯ ವಿಷಯಗಳ ಕೆಡುಕಿಗೆ ಅಂಟಿದವರು ಮುಳುಗುತ್ತಾರೆ, ಅನಾಸಕ್ತನು ದಾಟುತ್ತಾನೆಂದು ಗುರು ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಮನಸ್ಸು, ಇಂದ್ರಿಯ ನಿಗ್ರಹಿಸಿದವನು ದೇವತೆಗಳಿಂದಲೂ ಪೂಜಿತನಾಗಿ ಸನಾತನ ಬ್ರಹ್ಮ ಪಡೆಯುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"गुरु कहते हैं कि इन्द्रिय-विषयों के दोषों में आसक्त प्राणी डूबते हैं और अनासक्त पार जाता है। मन और इन्द्रियों को वश में करने वाला देवताओं से भी पूजित होकर सनातन ब्रह्म को पाता है।","te":"ఇంద్రియ విషయాల దోషాలలో ఆసక్తులైనవారు మునుగుతారని, అనాసక్తుడు దాటతాడని గురువు చెబుతాడు. మనసు, ఇంద్రియాలను నిగ్రహించినవాడు దేవతలచే కూడా పూజింపబడి సనాతన బ్రహ్మను పొందుతాడు.","ta":"புலன் பொருட்களின் தீமைகளில் பற்றுடையோர் மூழ்குகின்றனர், பற்றற்றவன் கடக்கிறான் என்று குரு கூறுகிறார். மனத்தையும் புலன்களையும் அடக்கியவன் தேவராலும் வணங்கப்பட்டுச் சனாதன பிரம்மத்தை அடைகிறான்.","ml":"ഇന്ദ്രിയ വിഷയങ്ങളുടെ ദുഃഖങ്ങളിൽ ആസക്തരായവർ താഴുന്നുവെന്നും, ആസക്തിയില്ലാത്തവൻ കടന്നുപോകുന്നുവെന്നും ഗുരു പറയുന്നു. മനസ്സിനെയും ഇന്ദ്രിയങ്ങളെയും നിയന്ത്രിക്കുന്നവൻ ദേവന്മാരാലും ആദരിക്കപ്പെടുകയും നിത്യമായ ബ്രഹ്മത്തെ നേടുകയും ചെയ്യുന്നുവെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.208; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"मोक्षधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Mokshadharma Parva (Duties for liberation)","verses":[{"text":"गुरुरुवाच","meaning":{"en":"The teacher said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"दुरन्तेष्विन्द्रियार्थेषु सक्ताः सीदन्ति जन्तवः ।\nये त्वसक्ता महात्मानस्ते यान्ति परमां गतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Creatures attached to sense objects, whose ends are bad, sink; but the great-souled who are unattached reach the highest goal."}},{"n":2,"text":"जन्ममृत्युजरादुःखैर्व्याधिभिर्मनसः क्लमैः ।\nदृष्ट्वेमं संततं लोकं घटेन्मोक्षाय बुद्धिमान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing this world ceaselessly beset by birth, death, old age, sorrow, disease and mental weariness, the wise man should strive for liberation."}},{"n":3,"text":"वाङ्मनोभ्यां शरीरेण शुचिः स्यादनहंकृतः ।\nप्रशान्तो ज्ञानवान्भिक्षुर्निरपेक्षश्चरेत्सुखम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Pure in speech, mind and body, free of ego, calm and knowing, a mendicant should wander happily, without expectation."}},{"n":4,"text":"अथ वा मनसः सङ्गं पश्येद्भूतानुकम्पया ।\nअत्राप्युपेक्षां कुर्वीत ज्ञात्वा कर्मफलं जगत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Or, from compassion for beings, he may notice the mind's attachment; even there he should stay indifferent, knowing the world to be the fruit of action."}},{"n":5,"text":"यत्कृतं प्राक्शुभं कर्म पापं वा तदुपाश्नुते ।\nतस्माच्छुभानि कर्माणि कुर्याद्वाग्बुद्धिकर्मभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whatever good or evil deed was done before, one receives its result; so one should do good deeds by speech, thought and action."}},{"n":6,"text":"अहिंसा सत्यवचनं सर्वभूतेषु चार्जवम् ।\nक्षमा चैवाप्रमादश्च यस्यैते स सुखी भवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Non-violence, truthful speech, uprightness to all beings, patience and carefulness: whoever has these becomes happy."}},{"n":7,"text":"यश्चैनं परमं धर्मं सर्वभूतसुखावहम् ।\nदुःखान्निःसरणं वेद स तत्त्वज्ञः सुखी भवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who knows this highest dharma, which brings happiness to all beings and a way out of sorrow, knows the truth and becomes happy."}},{"n":8,"text":"तस्मात्समाहितं बुद्ध्या मनो भूतेषु धारयेत् ।\nनापध्यायेन्न स्पृहयेन्नाबद्धं चिन्तयेदसत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Therefore one should hold the mind steady with understanding on living beings; one should not plot harm, not covet, and not think of what is untrue or unfounded."}},{"n":9,"text":"अवाग्योगप्रयोगेण मनोज्ञं संप्रवर्तते ।\nविवक्षता वा सद्वाक्यं धर्मं सूक्ष्ममवेक्षता ।\nसत्यां वाचमहिंस्रां च वदेदनपवादिनीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"What pleases the mind comes about through the practice of speech-discipline. One who wishes to speak, looking to the subtle dharma, should say good words: true, harmless and blameless speech."}},{"n":10,"text":"कल्कापेतामपरुषामनृशंसामपैशुनाम् ।\nईदृगल्पं च वक्तव्यमविक्षिप्तेन चेतसा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Speech free of fault, not harsh, not cruel, not slanderous: a little of such speech should be spoken with an untroubled mind."}},{"n":11,"text":"वाक्प्रबुद्धो हि संरागाद्विरागाद्व्याहरेद्यदि ।\nबुद्ध्या ह्यनिगृहीतेन मनसा कर्म तामसम् ।\nरजोभूतैर्हि करणैः कर्मणा प्रतिपद्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"If one aware of speech speaks from attachment or aversion, with a mind not held by understanding, the act is of tamas; with senses turned to rajas, one comes to such action."}},{"n":12,"text":"स दुःखं प्राप्य लोकेऽस्मिन्नरकायोपपद्यते ।\nतस्मान्मनोवाक्शरीरैराचरेद्धैर्यमात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having met suffering in this world, he goes toward hell. Therefore one should keep steadiness of oneself in mind, speech and body."}},{"n":13,"text":"प्रकीर्णमेषभारो हि यद्वद्धार्येत दस्युभिः ।\nप्रतिलोमां दिशं बुद्ध्वा संसारमबुधास्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"As a flock of scattered sheep is driven off by robbers, in a wrong direction, so do the unwise drive themselves into rebirth."}},{"n":14,"text":"तानेव च यथा दस्यून्क्षिप्त्वा गच्छेच्छिवां दिशम् ।\nतथा रजस्तमःकर्माण्युत्सृज्य प्राप्नुयात्सुखम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As one would throw off those robbers and go to a safe direction, so, casting off actions of rajas and tamas, one reaches happiness."}},{"n":15,"text":"निःसंदिग्धमनीहो वै मुक्तः सर्वपरिग्रहैः ।\nविविक्तचारी लघ्वाशी तपस्वी नियतेन्द्रियः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Free of doubt and desire, released from all possessions, living in solitude, eating lightly, austere and with senses restrained,"}},{"n":16,"text":"ज्ञानदग्धपरिक्लेशः प्रयोगरतिरात्मवान् ।\nनिष्प्रचारेण मनसा परं तदधिगच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"with afflictions burnt away by knowledge, delighting in practice, self-possessed, with a mind that no longer wanders, one reaches that Supreme."}},{"n":17,"text":"धृतिमानात्मवान्बुद्धिं निगृह्णीयादसंशयम् ।\nमनो बुद्ध्या निगृह्णीयाद्विषयान्मनसात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The steady, self-possessed man should restrain the intellect without doubt; he should restrain the mind with the intellect, and the objects with the mind of the self."}},{"n":18,"text":"निगृहीतेन्द्रियस्यास्य कुर्वाणस्य मनो वशे ।\nदेवतास्ताः प्रकाशन्ते हृष्टा यान्ति तमीश्वरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When one has restrained the senses and brought the mind under control, those deities appear and, pleased, go to that lord."}},{"n":19,"text":"ताभिः संसक्तमनसो ब्रह्मवत्संप्रकाशते ।\nएतैश्चापगतैः सर्वैर्ब्रह्मभूयाय कल्पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"One whose mind is joined with them shines like Brahman; and with all these gone, he becomes fit for oneness with Brahman."}},{"n":20,"text":"अथ वा न प्रवर्तेत योगतन्त्रैरुपक्रमेत् ।\nयेन तन्त्रमयं तन्त्रं वृत्तिः स्यात्तत्तदाचरेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Or one may not set out, and instead proceed by the methods of yoga; whatever method makes one's livelihood, that one should follow."}},{"n":21,"text":"कणपिण्याककुल्माषशाकयावकसक्तवः ।\nतथा मूलफलं भैक्षं पर्यायेणोपयोजयेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Grain-bits, oil-cake, kulmasha, greens, barley gruel and flour, as well as roots, fruits and alms, he may use in turn."}},{"n":22,"text":"आहारं नियतं चैव देशे काले च सात्त्विकम् ।\nतत्परीक्ष्यानुवर्तेत यत्प्रवृत्त्यनुवर्तकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"His food should be regulated, sattvic, suited to place and time; having examined it, he should follow what supports his progress."}},{"n":23,"text":"प्रवृत्तं नोपरुन्धेत शनैरग्निमिवेन्धयेत् ।\nज्ञानेन्धितं ततो ज्ञानमर्कवत्संप्रकाशते ॥","meaning":{"en":"He should not block what has begun, but kindle it slowly like a fire; kindled by knowledge, knowledge then shines like the sun."}},{"n":24,"text":"ज्ञानाधिष्ठानमज्ञानं त्रीँल्लोकानधितिष्ठति ।\nविज्ञानानुगतं ज्ञानमज्ञानादपकृष्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ignorance, resting on knowledge, stands over the three worlds; knowledge, accompanied by discernment, is drawn away from ignorance."}},{"n":25,"text":"पृथक्त्वात्संप्रयोगाच्च नासूयुर्वेद शाश्वतम् ।\nस तयोरपवर्गज्ञो वीतरागो विमुच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Through separateness and through union, one who is not envious knows the eternal; knowing the separation of the two, free of attachment, he is liberated."}},{"n":26,"text":"वयोतीतो जरामृत्यू जित्वा ब्रह्म सनातनम् ।\nअमृतं तदवाप्नोति यत्तदक्षरमव्ययम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Past the stage of age, having conquered old age and death, he gains the eternal Brahman, the immortal, which is the imperishable and unchanging."}}]}]}